  "digest": "# HEALTHCARE \u2014 2026-W46 (week to 2026-11-14)\n\n## Coverage changes\nSeven HOSPITALS initiations published 12\u2011Nov: DVLA (SELL, Rp938), HEAL (SELL, Rp259), KAEF (SELL, Rp206), KLBF (BUY, Rp1,044), MERK (BUY, Rp4,705), PRDA (BUY, Rp4,851) and PYFA (SELL, Rp32). SIDO (tempo\u2011scan) parked pending sign\u2011off after QC vetted; SILO and MIKA are parked awaiting QC; INAF and PEHA are in revision after a SECTOR_LEAD_HEALTHCARE return [coverage state].\n\n## Deck moves\nMacro deck\u2019s forward path unchanged since 7\u2011Nov review (usd_idr FY2027E 18,350, DXY 102.25, BI\u2011Rate 5.75%, CPI 3.28%, GDP 5.29%) [deck macro]. Spot marks refreshed to 13\u2011Nov: USD/IDR Rp18,190 and DXY 103.233. The `balance_of_payments_pressure` / CAUTIOUS regime tilts AVOID IDR\u2011rate\u2011sensitive names \u2014 neutral for healthcare. No healthcare\u2011specific drivers (BPJ rates, regulation changes) moved in the week.\n\n## Material news\nINAF partners with IPB to develop herbal products [triage e411235e]; that project is not yet in the DCF. KLBF fined by OJK for related\u2011party transaction violations [093f4d77], also named in a broader BUMN\u2011violations list (ADHI, ADCP, KLBF, others) [f3ef5ec8]; the penalty is booked in LK and priced. SIDO reported 9M\u20112026 net profit down 24.36% [cfa5b8b4]. IPO pipeline shows healthcare\u2011sector dominance among 9 candidates [e5bb4a4a].\n\n## What to watch\nBatch of three HOSPITALS (SIDO, MIKA, SILO) parked at QC \u2014 will they clear sign\u2011off and publish by next week? INAF and PEHA revisions need analyst answers to the SECTOR_LEAD\u2019s material challenges before push to QC. Any OJK follow\u2011up on affiliate\u2011transaction penalties; and any BPJ tariff changes (multiple reports circulating but no published decree). Coverage queue: MDLA and SOHO (pharma/hospital) at sign\u2011off await desk review.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
